{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/pulls/3683","id":4558226945,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPuAjtM8AAAABD7EGAQ","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/pull/3683","diff_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/pull/3683.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/pull/3683.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/issues/3683","number":3683,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(OMN-18567): schedule the convergence of the deploy runner's private clone tree","user":{"login":"jonahgabriel","id":1002253,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDIyNTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1002253?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel","html_url":"https://github.com/jonahgabriel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Ticket: **OMN-18567** (child of OMN-16964). The one-time repair landed earlier today and is recorded on the ticket with per-clone before/after shas. This PR is the **recurrence** half, which is what the ticket is actually for.\n\n## The problem\n\n`/data/omninode/runner_omni_home` is the deploy runner's own `OMNI_HOME`: bind-mounted into `omninode-deploy-runner` at an identical host path, owned by the runner uid, and the build source the dev-lane refresh, the stability-lane refresh and the release-train tag cut all read.\n\nNothing converged it. On 2026-09-17 five of its six clones were on detached HEADs and every one of the six was behind `origin/dev`:\n\n| clone | behind |\n|---|---|\n| onex_change_control | 1120 |\n| omnibase_infra | 294 |\n| omnimarket | 171 |\n| omnibase_core | 30 |\n| omnibase_spi | 5 |\n| omnibase_compat | 3 |\n\nNeither existing mechanism on that host reaches the tree, and both miss it by design. The `:37` maintenance sync converges host-resident **files** and touches no git clone. The `:19` workspace reconcile is scoped to the shared operator-owned tree. The tree's own provisioning helper clones when a clone is **missing** and never advances one that already exists, so the tree moved only as a side effect of refresh runs fetching for their own purposes.\n\nPer CLAUDE.md rule 5, a repair nobody schedules is advisory.\n\n## What lands\n\n- **`deploy/maintenance/omninode-runner-tree-converge.sh`** — a tick in the shape of its two siblings. It decides *when* a converge may run, *which* clones it covers and *what* is receipted. Every repair is delegated to omniclaude's `converge-canonical-clone.sh`, the one sanctioned converger; none of its preserve-then-reset behaviour is re-implemented here.\n- **`deploy/maintenance/cron.d/omninode-runner-tree-converge`** — hourly at `:49`, clear of the `*/15` system report, the `:19` reconcile and the `:37` sync.\n- **Both files added to the host-artifact MANIFEST.** That *is* the installation. The hourly `--converge` writes every entry that differs from `origin/dev` and reads it back, so this reaches the host by merging to `dev` — no crontab is edited by hand.\n- **A collector in the system Slack reporter**, folded into the existing reporter rather than built as a second alerter, so it inherits that script's Slack poster, per-key de-duplication, resolved-notification and `*/15` cron.\n\n## The clone set is the tree, not a list\n\nDiscovery is every direct child with a `.git` **directory** (a worktree carries a `.git` file and is never converged). A hand-maintained repo list is the OMN-15137 defect, and it would be wrong today: `sibling_clone_manifest.sh` names five repos and this tree holds six, because `onex_change_control` arrives by a different path.\n\n## AC2 — the busy gate, and one deliberate departure from `deploy-runners.sh`\n\nThree host-local signals decide, and they do not have equal standing.\n\n**Idle proof (required, must read as a clean zero):** `docker top omninode-deploy-runner | grep -c Runner.Worker`. That container is the only one with the tree mounted — the verify runner shares the runner group and is deliberately built without the bind. `docker top` is daemon-side and creates no process in the container, which matters because a bare `docker exec` there defaults to root and has already left root-owned files under a job workspace.\n\nAn **empty** answer is UNKNOWN, never zero. `| grep -c X || true` exits 0 with no output when the container is gone or the daemon errors, and reading that as \"zero workers\" is the fail-open shape documented at `scripts/deploy-runners.sh:1141` as having killed a live job once already.\n\n**Vetoes (a hit refuses; an absence proves nothing):** a process whose cwd or open fd resolves inside the tree — the only signal that sees an out-of-band writer, since anyone hand-running a lane refresh with `OMNI_HOME` pointed here is invisible to the container probe — and an in-flight git operation, using the marker set `scripts/git-gc-auto.sh:76` already uses.\n\n**The GitHub `busy` flag is deliberately not consulted.** Root on the lab host holds no credential with that scope: `gh` as root is unauthenticated, and the operator env file's token returns `403 Resource not accessible by personal access token` on `/orgs/OmniNode-ai/actions/runners` (verified live 2026-09-17). The only working credential is one person's personal oauth token, and a scheduled mechanism that depends on that fails silently the day it expires. Requiring a signal that cannot be obtained would make every tick refuse forever, which is AC1 unreachable dressed as caution. The worker probe answers the question that matters here — *is something running in the container that holds the tree* — where the GitHub flag answers *is a job assigned*.\n\n**The irreducible race is stated, not hidden.** The runner can accept a queued job at any instant and nothing on the host can hold it off; `deploy-runners.sh` documents the same window even with both signals. It is bounded by re-running the gate immediately before **each** clone and aborting the rest of the run the moment it changes, so at most one clone is exposed rather than six, and by running hourly rather than by the minute.\n\n## AC3 — ownership\n\ncron runs this as root; the tree is owned by the runner uid. A root converge rewrites working-tree files as root and leaves a tree the runner can no longer write, turning a stale clone into a broken one — strictly worse than the drift. Every command that touches the tree goes through `as_owner` from `scripts/reconcile_privilege_lib.sh`, sourced and never re-implemented. `scripts/check_reconciler_privilege.py` passes and now governs this file, since it discovers scripts by following cron-unit invocations through the manifest.\n\n## Receipts\n\nOne verdict line, to stdout and to the state file:\n\n```\nrunner-tree-converge|<VERDICT>|ts=|tree=|clones=|in_sync=|converged=|failed=|skipped=|reason=|last_success=|detail=\n```\n\n`detail` names every clone as `<name>:<before12>-><after12>`. `last_success` advances **only** on a completed run with nothing failed and nothing skipped. That is what keeps a permanently busy runner from reading as a permanently converged tree, and it is why exiting 0 on a refusal is safe: a refusal is the guard working, and paging on every busy tick is how a channel stops being read. The reporter ages that field rather than reading the latest verdict, so a single `REFUSED` does not page while a tree left unconverged for hours does.\n\nThe delegate's exit code is never the proof. Each clone's HEAD is re-read after the converger returns, and a clone that did not reach its upstream counts as FAILED even when the converger exited 0.\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/scripts/test_runner_tree_converge_omn18567.py` — 21 cases, RED before and GREEN after. Every refusal case asserts the clone **did not move**, not merely that the word REFUSED was printed: a guard that prints a refusal and converges anyway is the failure this class exists to end.\n\nSeven more cases in the reporter's own suite cover the collector: missing file warns, FAILED is critical, a fresh converge is OK, a single refusal does not reach *Active issues*, a stale `last_success` warns even while refusing, and an unparseable verdict warns rather than reading green.\n\nLocal: `106 passed` across this file, the reporter suite, both maintenance-sync suites, the clone-privilege suite and the workspace-reconcile cron suite. `check_reconciler_privilege.py` and `check_reconciler_movement_proof.py` both OK. Full `pre-commit run` on the changed files green.\n\n## Follow-through after merge\n\nThe `:37` sync installs both files on its next tick. The install readback — the cron entry as installed and the tick's first run verdict — goes on OMN-18567, and no AC is ticked before it.\n\n## Companion\n\nomniclaude#2217 closes the reattach residual recorded on the same ticket: the detached-HEAD derivation had no remote-default fallback, which is a real exposure for a tree nothing but machines touch.\n\nEvidence-Ticket: OMN-18567\nEvidence-Source: OCC#9985\n","created_at":"2026-09-17T12:08:05Z","updated_at":"2026-09-17T14:35:27Z","closed_at":"2026-09-17T14:35:26Z","merged_at":"2026-09-17T14:35:26Z","merge_commit_sha":"2a4e49511d421c368adb5097131c5d1b985272c3","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/pulls/3683/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/pulls/3683/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/issues/3683/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/statuses/b9ae5c2e995be7efadbb8b1071ee9c8ebf7ca210","head":{"label":"OmniNode-ai:jonah/omn-18567-runner-tree-converge-tick","ref":"jonah/omn-18567-runner-tree-converge-tick","sha":"b9ae5c2e995be7efadbb8b1071ee9c8ebf7ca210","user":{"login":"OmniNode-ai","id":209038818,"node_id":"O_kgDODHWt4g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/209038818?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmniNode-ai","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmniNode-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmniNode-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmniNode-ai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmniNode-ai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmniNode-ai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmniNode-ai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmniNode-ai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmniNode-ai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmniNode-ai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"repo":{"id":1054876596,"node_id":"R_kgDOPuAjtA","name":"omnibase_infra","full_name":"OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra","private":false,"owner":{"login":"OmniNode-ai","id":209038818,"node_id":"O_kgDODHWt4g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/209038818?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/OmniNode-ai","html_url":"https: